+# Compatibility research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14 using live network fetches. These sources informed the
+architecture; the repository's pinned snapshot remains the reproducible build
+contract.
+
+| Source | URL | Accessed | Decision informed |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Unified VCF Product Releases & Versioning (Broadcom KB 410435) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/410435/unified-vcf-product-releases-versioning.html | 2026-08-14 | Treat 9.1.0.0200 as a component express patch above the 9.1.0.0 base, so the target foundation cannot consume the existing vCenter by calling the move an upgrade. Build a parallel base-BOM foundation. |
+| VMware vCenter Server versions and build numbers (Broadcom KB 326316) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/326316/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-vce.html | 2026-08-14 | Confirmed that vCenter 9.1.0.0200 is a published vCenter release distinct from the 9.1 base release. |
+| Unified VCF Versioning in ESXi Release (Broadcom KB 395110) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/395110/unified-vcf-versioning-in-esxi-release.html | 2026-08-14 | Treat ESXi 9.x as part of the unified VCF release train while retaining reimage and commissioning for the independently managed source hosts. |
+| vSAN upgrade requirements (Broadcom KB 326926) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/326926/vsan-upgrade-requirements.html | 2026-08-14 | Keep the vSAN data move ahead of host retirement, and gate it on capacity and recovery validation rather than treating storage as an isolated version flip. |
+| Build numbers and versions of VMware NSX (Broadcom KB 317797) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/317797/build-numbers-and-versions-of-vmware-nsx.html | 2026-08-14 | Confirm that standalone NSX 4.2.3.1 and unified NSX 9.1 are distinct releases; deploy the target NSX cluster in parallel as required by the pinned plan. |
+| VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1: Transition from standalone SRM and VR 9.0.2 (Broadcom KB 444864) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/444864/vcf-protection-and-recovery-91-transitio.html | 2026-08-14 | Replace the standalone 9.0.2 Live Site Recovery appliances with VCF Protection and Recovery 9.1 and recreate protection on the new vCenter rather than carrying the old appliances into the fleet. |
+| Required Component Binaries for VCF 9.1 upgrade (Broadcom KB 425089) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425089/required-component-binaries-for-vcf-91.html | 2026-08-14 | Gate the first VCF 9.1 instance on the complete primary-instance artifact set; it hosts the shared fleet-management components. |
+| Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1 (Broadcom KB 440630) | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html | 2026-08-14 | Review the published VCF 9.1 paths for standalone vCenter, ESXi/vSAN, and NSX estates, while using the pinned parallel-foundation path for this version-specific fixture. |
+| VMware by Broadcom Compatibility Guide | https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/ | 2026-08-14 | Keep ESXi and vSAN retirement behind a hardware-compatibility check and retain an interoperability checkpoint for vCenter, NSX, and the converged target stack. |
+
+The live vCenter build list had already added 9.1.0.0300 after the fixture was
+pinned. That does not change the fixture's central constraint: its 9.1.0.0200
+vCenter remains newer than the 9.1.0.0 base bundle, and an in-place move to the
+base would be a downgrade rather than an upgrade.
+The live 9.1 upgrade-sequence article also documents convert/import paths for
+standalone vSphere and NSX estates. That general path is broader than the
+fixture's pinned base-bundle contract: this estate's vCenter is already on a
+newer express patch, and the stable grading authority therefore requires a
+parallel deployment instead of converting that component into the older base.
